WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.469 --> 00:00:03.839
- The last time I ate a
stick of unsalted butter,

00:00:03.839 --> 00:00:05.597
I feel like I was like 10 and I realized

00:00:05.597 --> 00:00:09.180
that this is not the
way to live your life.

00:00:10.131 --> 00:00:12.193
(upbeat music)

00:00:12.193 --> 00:00:14.671
- When I was a kid, I
used to drink A1 sauce

00:00:14.671 --> 00:00:15.978
straight from the bottle.

00:00:15.978 --> 00:00:18.145
No one ever knew that
this is something I did

00:00:18.145 --> 00:00:20.769
until I was at the
refrigerator with the bottle

00:00:20.769 --> 00:00:23.267
up to my lips and my mom caught me.

00:00:23.267 --> 00:00:27.434
She threw away the A1 sauce
and never bought it again.

00:00:28.345 --> 00:00:29.775
And it burns a little bit going down,

00:00:29.775 --> 00:00:31.075
I remember that a little bit.

00:00:31.075 --> 00:00:33.654
I don't think I'll go back to
doing this regularly at all.

00:00:33.654 --> 00:00:35.364
But it's still good.

00:00:35.364 --> 00:00:36.578
One more for the road.

00:00:36.578 --> 00:00:37.472
- I can't remember the last time I ate

00:00:37.472 --> 00:00:39.161
Arby's sauce out of a packet.

00:00:39.161 --> 00:00:41.614
I think in middle school I
tried to be a little less weird

00:00:41.614 --> 00:00:43.697
so probably age 11 or 12.

00:00:46.321 --> 00:00:47.465
Yeah, it was pretty bad.

00:00:47.465 --> 00:00:48.748
It would be worth it if I went to Arby's

00:00:48.748 --> 00:00:51.427
and got another sandwich
and put the sauce on it.

00:00:51.427 --> 00:00:53.100
But yeah, no, I'm not
feeling great about that.

00:00:53.100 --> 00:00:56.652
- The last time I ate a
stick of unsalted butter,

00:00:56.652 --> 00:00:58.558
I feel like I was like 10 and I realized

00:00:58.558 --> 00:01:00.376
that this is not the
way to live your life.

00:01:00.376 --> 00:01:03.944
In Indian culture, we have
this one god, Krishna,

00:01:03.944 --> 00:01:06.912
and he eats butter,
and all my comic books,

00:01:06.912 --> 00:01:08.886
they would talk about him
grabbing the fresh butter

00:01:08.886 --> 00:01:11.244
that was just churned
from the milk of cows.

00:01:11.244 --> 00:01:13.055
So I went to my fridge, tried some butter,

00:01:13.055 --> 00:01:16.001
and I was like, "That is the stuff."

00:01:16.001 --> 00:01:17.391
It tastes like creamy nothing.

00:01:17.391 --> 00:01:18.434
I do not like this.

00:01:18.434 --> 00:01:19.974
Maybe it's different if
it's fresh from a cow,

00:01:19.974 --> 00:01:22.197
but this is like the fridge
of Costco or something.

00:01:22.197 --> 00:01:24.357
- I used to eat mashed avocados in milk

00:01:24.357 --> 00:01:26.397
with condensed milk and ice.

00:01:26.397 --> 00:01:29.571
My mom actually did this for
me when I was growing up.

00:01:29.571 --> 00:01:31.902
I don't know if it's like
a specific Filipino thing

00:01:31.902 --> 00:01:33.664
or something she just liked to do,

00:01:33.664 --> 00:01:36.136
but I just grew to love it.

00:01:36.136 --> 00:01:39.013
See, that's really good, that's
family recipe right there.

00:01:39.013 --> 00:01:41.225
What I would say to my old self is,

00:01:41.225 --> 00:01:42.386
"You did it right with this."

00:01:42.386 --> 00:01:45.339
- I used to pack a bag of
salt in a clear Ziploc bag

00:01:45.339 --> 00:01:47.189
and just bring it to
school and people thought

00:01:47.189 --> 00:01:50.845
I was doing drugs, but it's
actually just a bag of salt.

00:01:50.845 --> 00:01:52.554
The reason why I stopped is because

00:01:52.554 --> 00:01:55.871
my blood pressure was getting super high.

00:01:55.871 --> 00:01:57.550
I was always dehydrated.

00:01:57.550 --> 00:01:59.564
This feels so good, but at the same time,

00:01:59.564 --> 00:02:02.647
I'm like, "What the heck am I doing?"

00:02:03.754 --> 00:02:04.912
Oh my gosh.

00:02:04.912 --> 00:02:06.235
Yeah, I would never do that again now,

00:02:06.235 --> 00:02:07.839
it's like strictly in the past.

00:02:07.839 --> 00:02:10.072
Hey Mom, I'm sorry, I used to eat salt.

00:02:10.072 --> 00:02:12.617
I know that you always
told me that's not good,

00:02:12.617 --> 00:02:13.763
too bad, I already did it.

00:02:13.763 --> 00:02:16.429
- I used to eat a ton
of gross shit as a kid,

00:02:16.429 --> 00:02:19.721
but my ultimate favorite is tomato sauce

00:02:19.721 --> 00:02:22.306
or ketchup on white rice.

00:02:22.306 --> 00:02:24.143
I think I discovered it by chance one day

00:02:24.143 --> 00:02:27.296
'cause I like to dip most
things in tomato sauce,

00:02:27.296 --> 00:02:31.453
but then when I put the rice
with it, I was just blown away.

00:02:31.453 --> 00:02:33.821
I think we all have weird
things that we enjoy,

00:02:33.821 --> 00:02:36.383
I'm sure there are better-tasting
things in the world,

00:02:36.383 --> 00:02:39.331
technically, but this is just
really comforting for me.

00:02:39.331 --> 00:02:41.744
I crave this as an adult almost every day.

00:02:41.744 --> 00:02:43.055
It's the sad truth.

00:02:43.055 --> 00:02:46.305
- Oh my gosh, this feels so nostalgic.

